rd progress. Words: sculpt, prop, breath phrase, tempo, texture, accuracy. Showing: site phrases in the school's own spaces (a hall, steps with no jumping, a yard), for another class. End-of-unit evidence (two check days), id by id: DA:Pr4.1.8a, a guide look-for on the showing: shapes sculpted around a partner, a prop and a room feature, with eye focus held through the pattern; DA:Pr4.1.8b, a show item at the teacher's spot: a phrase with feet and arms in separate tempos and one breath phrase, its choice named; DA:Pr4.1.8c, a guide look-for on the showing: two textures of energy steered on purpose; DA:Pr5.1.8a, a show item: a spatial design and a rhythmic phrase copied from the teacher once and recalled; DA:Pr5.1.8b, a written item on the written day: the invented dancer's habits rated and one improvement planned for each; DA:Pr5.1.8c, the kept progress record (personal goal, practice entries, the change since the baseline), scored after the session. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: low partner balances and syncopation (Level 1). Tools: the layered-counts card, the props card, the habit rating card, the progress record, work cards, Curio Class's own; a beat keeper with two tempos or the printed counts card. Free path: chairs, scarves, a drum and claps. Once-a-week path: 8 sessions | First in grade 8 because it reopens the floor and the rehearsal routine and moves the elements to space around people and places and to layered time; the personal progress record carries through the year. Physical education's grade 8 dance routine unit (its unit 18, weeks 14 to 16) and health's habits project (its unit 26, weeks 18 to 22) come later in the year | Candidate: a site dance by a living maker from Asia or Latin America beside Juice | Hazards and controls: site phrases only on level ground the teacher has checked; steps and stairs used for shapes, never for jumping; props light, chairs stable and never stood on; no lifts; the class stays in sight. Sabar: the se