warm-up, cool-down and room-back fit the rest of the 40 minutes, and each student has at most one show item after
the group's turn. Every student's evidence is collected once in a window; no item is scored twice. Days above are
band course days (year 7 starts on day 65, year 8 on day 129). The mid-year checks fall on school days 83 and 85 of
each grade's year, off every core check week; the year-end checks fall in week 32, the finals week.

## Cross-subject

The three dance technique rows of the band carry leans on physical education, da-g8-technique also on health,
da-g6-respond and da-g8-respond on ELA, and da-g6-connect on social studies (data/progressions/arts.csv). STANDARD.md 6
splits dance and physical education: physical education teaches dance sequences as motor skill, this course
teaches dance as an art. Each contact below has its "if later" line; ELA and social studies are core courses, while
physical education and health are after-core courses named by their own frames (lesson 32: this course assumes no
motor cue or health step taught there).

### Physical education, grades 6 to 8 (same year, name each other)

The physical education 6 to 8 frame is written (2026-11-25); its units and weeks are cited from it and
data/plans/calendar.csv.

| This course's row and unit | Physical education's row and unit | What each teaches | If later |
|---|---|---|---|
| da-g6-technique, da-g6-elements (unit 1, grade 6 weeks 1 to 9); da-g6-form (unit 2, weeks 10 to 16) | g6-dance-sequences (unit 6, grade 6 weeks 22 to 27, its course days 66 to 79) | Physical education: eight-count phrases, transitions and four-phrase sequences in a range of styles as motor skill (tinikling, a line dance, a partner set dance); dance: partner and group spacing, accents, tension, a study with a goal | Dance teaches first; physical education unit 6 may retrieve the counts. Neither teaches the other's part, and the picks differ |
| da-g7-technique, da-g7-elements (unit 5, grade 7 weeks 1 to 9); da-g7-form (unit 6, weeks 10 to 16) | g7-dance-ideas (unit 13, grade 7 weeks 22 to 26, its course days 162 to 174) | Physical education: space, time, force and relationship used to change a line dance, a circle dance (kolo) and a rhythm form; dance: borrowed designs, accents, a study shaped with tools and forms and explained | Dance teaches first; physical education's unison, canon and contrast are its own movement ideas, and the dance course does not teach them as motor skill |
| da-g8-technique, da-g8-elements (unit 9, grade 8 weeks 1 to 9) | g8-fitness-dance-apply (unit 18, grade 8 weeks 14 to 16, its course days 233 to 240) | Physical education: a dance routine with good form in a planned week; dance: recalled spatial and rhythmic phrases, layered tempos, personal goals on dance skill | Dance teaches first; if a school runs physical education earlier, the dance unit still teaches only the art |

