347: ## Cross-subject
348: 
349: The three dance technique rows of the band carry leans on physical education, da-g8-technique also on health,
350: da-g6-respond and da-g8-respond on ELA, and da-g6-connect on social studies (data/progressions/arts.csv). STANDARD.md 6
351: splits dance and physical education: physical education teaches dance sequences as motor skill, this course
352: teaches dance as an art. Each contact below has its "if later" line; ELA and social studies are core courses, while
353: physical education and health are after-core courses named by their own frames (lesson 32: this course assumes no
354: motor cue or health step taught there).
