pins not tried (turns kept to one slow turn in place); floor checked. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
324: | 8 | 7 | Where styles come from. *What does a dance style's history tell us about its spirit, and why do dances from different places differ?* | 14 | da-g7-stage; da-g7-connect | DA:Pr6.1.7a; DA:Pr6.1.7b; DA:Cn10.1.7a; DA:Cn10.1.7b; DA:Cn11.1.7a | Performing (Pr6); connecting (Cn10, Cn11); responding practiced on the works (review). Works: capoeira (Brazil, made by enslaved Africans and their descendants; on UNESCO's list of intangible cultural heritage since 2014 as the capoeira circle), described and linked to UNESCO's page; Argentine tango (Buenos Aires and Montevideo, late 1800s; on UNESCO's list since 2009), described and linked to UNESCO's page; Rosy Simas, Weave (Seneca Nation; Rosy Simas Danse, Minneapolis, 2018; the unit plan records whether living, as of its date), a dance made with Native and other dancers about belonging, described and linked to the company's page, watched only | Retrieval in day 2's warm-up: grade 6 manners, notes and production terms (da-g6-stage, unit 4) and the viewpoint dance and cultural meaning (da-g6-connect, unit 4). DA:Pr6.1.7a: recommend adaptations to the performing space, follow etiquette, keep a rehearsal journal and apply the choreographer's notes. DA:Pr6.1.7b: explore producing the dance for another venue or audience (the gym, outdoors, a younger class) and explain how production elements would change. DA:Cn10.1.7a: contrast movement qualities across two styles with the student's own, or with an invented dancer's, marked the same, and discuss how each shows a perspective. DA:Cn10.1.7b: research a style's history from the class list (capoeira, tango, tap, ballet, hip-hop) on the research card, and present a study of its spirit made of the student's own moves, never an imitation of the style. DA:Cn11.1.7a: compare dances from different places (capoeira and tango, or tango and Weave) and suggest why the differences developed. Words: venue, journal, history, spirit, perspective, tradition. Showing: the spirit studies for families, with the family's yes for any showing outside class. End-of-unit evidence (two check days), id by id: DA:Pr6.1.7a, a guide look-for on the family showing (a space adaptation used, etiquette kept, a note applied), with the kept rehearsal journal; DA:Pr6.1.7b, the kept venue card: one other venue or audience and two production elements that would change, with reasons; DA:Cn10.1.7a, a written item on the written day: two styles' qualities contrasted with the student's or the invented dancer's, and the perspective each shows; DA:Cn10.1.7b, a guide look-for on the spirit study with the kept research card (two sources, the history in three lines); DA:Cn11.1.7a, a written item: two dances from different places compared, with one reason their differences developed. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: many cultures and eras analyzed (grade 8). Tools: the journal page, venue card, research card, work cards, Curio Class's own. Free path: printed source pages. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | Last in grade 7 because the family showing gathers the year's borrowed designs, studies and revisions, and a style's history needs unit 7's comparing of styles. Its family showing (weeks 30 and 31) is its own end-of-unit assessment, before the year-end check in week 32 | Candidate: the class list of styles checked for sources from each style's own community | Capoeira: the sensitivity agent reads UNESCO's page and an Afro-Brazilian or Brazilian cultural body's page first; slavery is told in plain sentences, with no role play of enslaved people or enslavers. Capoeira's kicks and sweeps are not tried; the spirit study keeps to the sway, the circle and call and response, with no move aimed at a person. Weave: watched only; the agent reads Rosy Simas Danse's own pages and a Seneca Nation source first; she is named as a Seneca maker, the dance is hers, and no student imitates its movement, a ceremony or regalia. Tango is studied by watching; any partner frame is by agreement, with a solo version. Health's steps if a student tells something. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
