# Arts progression: second read, 2026-11-21

Read: data/progressions/arts.csv (498 rows), the music Level 1 to 4 rows (mu-g9-invent to mu-g12-connect, 28 rows,
written 2026-11-21) against data/standards/ncas-performance-standards.txt and the words file, STANDARD.md 3.2 and 3.3,
APPROACH.md, the arts lens, docs/agents/EXPERT.md, and the first read (prework-arts-progression-read-2026-11-20.md,
finding 6). Later.csv L86 (finding 6 applied only to flagged rows) is the second task.

## Task 1: music Level 1 to 4 rows

Checked and fine: all 63 strand ids owned once (21 per level, Level 4 `~` only on `.IIIa`); each row's ids match its
thread; Level 1 bridge sentence on mu-g9-invent only, in the shared wording; review-unit sentence on mu-g10-invent and
mu-g11-invent; every row names its assessment; level verbs climb (describe, explain, analyze; teacher criteria, own
criteria, researched criteria); recording and sacred-work notes in the settled wording; no instrument assumed.

- mu-g12-criticism: owns `~MU:Re8.1.C.IIIa` but did not assume its owner mu-g11-express. Decision: added to assumes,
  and mu-g12-criticism added to mu-g11-express hands_on.
- mu-g12-connect: owns `~MU:Cn11.0.C.IIIa` but did not assume its owner mu-g11-respond. Decision: added to assumes,
  and mu-g12-connect added to mu-g11-respond hands_on.
- mu-g12-perform: the only grade 12 showing row without the 18-or-over sentence the other four disciplines carry.
  Decision: added "A student of 18 or over gives their own yes to be shown or recorded; otherwise the family does."
- mu-g11-respond: dropped "advanced" from `MU:Re9.1.C.IIIa`, so Level 3 read the same as Level 2. Decision: restored.
- mu-g9-choose, mu-g10-choose, mu-g11-choose: no row said model pieces come from more than one culture and era (lens,
  "Works from many times and places"). Decision: one sentence added to each choose row.
- mu-g9 to mu-g11 owner rows (24): first sentences were the words lines strung together. Decision: reworded in task 2.
- "where level 1/level 2" in What changes lines is lowercase; the file uses lowercase in 35 lines across disciplines.
  Decision: left (house form in this file).
- model ids (`rhythm-syllables` carried into Level 1 to 4 read rows): odd name for score analysis, but a valid model
  chain. Decision: left; the frame may rename the model.

## Task 2: notes that track the words file (L86)

Test: share of a note's first-sentence words (stop words removed) found in its owned ids' words lines. Before: mean
0.81, 309 rows at 0.8 or more, 167 at 0.9 or more. Every row at 0.8 or more, and the 24 music Level 1 to 3 owner rows,
had its first sentence reworded as the unit task (what the student makes or does: a log, a sketch, a critique, a
dance study, a scene, a map), keeping every owned id's action. Fifteen rows still at 0.85 or more after the first
pass were reworded again. After: mean 0.57, 19 rows at 0.8 or more, 1 at 0.9 or more (the remaining ones name
concrete dance elements or production steps whose words cannot be avoided). What changes lines, assessments, teacher
notes, ids, owners and grades were not changed.

