ty; hard history (slavery in Brazil) taught plainly in the case card, never role played; no costume, no music used as a joke; the circle's master and ritual roles are named, not imitated. Spot-checked 2026-11-25: UNESCO's Representative List entry "Capoeira circle" (https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/capoeira-circle-00892, inscribed 2014) describes the circle as open to people of any gender; it does not say whether it is taught in schools, so the agent studies a Brazilian national heritage institute's page and a capoeira group's own teaching page first. Naadam not spot-checked: the agent checks it at UNESCO's entry or swaps it. Swap allowed. Cost: $0 |
